<!-- The Bankr. D. Kan. memorandum's Word styles: the cross-engine recipe (tools/fb/src/docxxengine.rs) in the face of
     the typst template ({font}, Times New Roman; no D. Kan. rule names a face) at 16 pt (size 32 half points: D. Kan.
     LBR 9004.1(a)(1), 12 pt or larger and no more than 12 characters per inch on average); Body Text in exact 32 pt
     line boxes (typst pitch-double, LBR 9004.1(a)(1) double spaced: two type sizes) with a half-inch indent; the
     counsel, court, caption, title, heading, table, quotation and signature lines in 18.4 pt boxes (typst
     pitch-single, 1.15 x the size); letter page with 1-inch margins. docx/ksb-motion-brief.lua writes every
     paragraph's own spacing and the one section: every page numbered from the first, the cover included (LBR
     9004.1(a)(2)), the number centered at the bottom, its line 645 twips above the page foot (where typst sets its
     18.4 pt line box, footer-descent 30 %). The markdown is read as CommonMark, as cmarker reads it. Twips: 20 x pt. -->
